      {"type":"mc","q":"True or false: “Inherited traits are always learned by practice” correctly answers “Several generations of plants show similar flower color even when grown by different gardeners. Which reasoning produces the most defensible conclusion.”","choices":["True","False"],"answer":"False","explain":"The statement is false. Inherited physical traits are passed from parents to offspring through biological information This conclusion accounts for every condition in the challenge. The correct answer is \"Inherited physical traits are passed from parents to offspring through biological information,\" not \"Inherited traits are always learned by practice.\"","audio":"True or false: “Inherited traits are always learned by practice” correctly answers “Several generations of plants show similar flower color even when grown by different gardeners. Which reasoning produces the most defensible conclusion.”"},
      {"type":"mc","q":"Two identical plants grow to different heights when one receives less light and water. Which reasoning produces the most defensible conclusion?","choices":["Acquired physical traits develop during an organism's life because of experience, use, injury, or environment","Acquired traits are automatically passed to every offspring","Acquired traits exist before birth in all cases","A species must share every acquired trait"],"answer":"Acquired physical traits develop during an organism's life because of experience, use, injury, or environment","explain":"Acquired physical traits develop during an organism's life because of experience, use, injury, or environment This conclusion accounts for every condition in the challenge.","audio":"Two identical plants grow to different heights when one receives less light and water. Which reasoning produces the most defensible conclusion?"},
      {"type":"mc","q":"A claim about a bird's damaged beak must be tested against family traits and injury history. Which reasoning produces the most defensible conclusion?","choices":["One organism can establish a species-wide pattern","Comparing parents, offspring, and environmental history helps classify a trait as inherited or acquired","Environmental records cannot help classify traits","Appearance alone always proves how a trait developed"],"answer":"Comparing parents, offspring, and environmental history helps classify a trait as inherited or acquired","explain":"Comparing parents, offspring, and environmental history helps classify a trait as inherited or acquired This conclusion accounts for every condition in the challenge.","audio":"A claim about a bird's damaged beak must be tested against family traits and injury history. Which reasoning produces the most defensible conclusion?"},
      {"type":"mc","q":"A trained route and natural wing structure must be sorted into behavior and physical-trait evidence. Which reasoning produces the most defensible conclusion?","choices":["Every behavior is an inherited physical trait","A learned behavior is acquired through experience, while an inherited physical trait is a body feature present because of heredity","Practice changes heredity immediately","Body structures are learned behaviors"],"answer":"A learned behavior is acquired through experience, while an inherited physical trait is a body feature present because of heredity","explain":"A learned behavior is acquired through experience, while an inherited physical trait is a body feature present because of heredity This conclusion accounts for every condition in the challenge.","audio":"A trained route and natural wing structure must be sorted into behavior and physical-trait evidence. Which reasoning produces the most defensible conclusion?"},
      {"type":"mc","q":"True or false: “An organism's observed features can reflect inherited information, environmental conditions, or both” correctly answers “Siblings share several body features but differ in scars and muscle development after different experiences. Which reasoning produces the most defensible conclusion.”","choices":["True","False"],"answer":"True","explain":"The statement is true. An organism's observed features can reflect inherited information, environmental conditions, or both This conclusion accounts for every condition in the challenge.","audio":"True or false: “An organism's observed features can reflect inherited information, environmental conditions, or both” correctly answers “Siblings share several body features but differ in scars and muscle development after different experiences. Which reasoning produces the most defensible conclusion.”"},
      {"type":"mc","q":"Which answer correctly resolves “Several generations of plants show similar flower color even when grown by different gardeners. Which reasoning produces the most defensible conclusion” and replaces the incorrect choice “Inherited traits are always learned by practice”?","choices":["Inherited physical traits are passed from parents to offspring through biological information","Organisms choose inherited traits after birth","Every inherited trait is caused by an accident","Inherited traits are always learned by practice"],"answer":"Inherited physical traits are passed from parents to offspring through biological information","explain":"Inherited physical traits are passed from parents to offspring through biological information is the defensible answer. Inherited physical traits are passed from parents to offspring through biological information This conclusion accounts for every condition in the challenge. The response \"Inherited traits are always learned by practice\" fails at least one condition, so the correction uses the complete sci lesson evidence.","audio":"Which answer correctly resolves “Several generations of plants show similar flower color even when grown by different gardeners. Which reasoning produces the most defensible conclusion” and replaces the incorrect choice “Inherited traits are always learned by practice”?"}
